/*!

\page arcstk-parse

\brief Parse responses from AccurateRip

\version @PROJECT_VERSION@



\section parse_syno SYNOPSIS

arcstk-parse [OPTIONS] FILENAME


\section parse_desc DESCRIPTION

Parse AccurateRip database responses; print output checksums, confidence values,
and the frame 450 checksums for each block in the response.


\section parse_opts OPTIONS

\subsection parse_opts_out Options for output

\par \--format=FORMAT
Specify the output format. FORMAT must be one of: \b json, \b text,
\b text_decorated, \b raw, \b yaml. The default is \b text_decorated. If omitted
or specified without a value, the default is applied.

\snippet{doc} include/option_help.dox      OPT_HELP

\snippet{doc} include/option_logfile.dox   OPT_LOGFILE

\snippet{doc} include/option_outfile.dox   OPT_OUTFILE

\snippet{doc} include/option_quiet.dox     OPT_QUIET

\snippet{doc} include/option_verbosity.dox OPT_VERBOSITY

\snippet{doc} include/option_version.dox   OPT_VERSION


\section parse_exmp EXAMPLES

Parse the binary data returned by AccurateRip and print it in a human-readable
form:

\code{.sh}$ arcstk-parse dBAR-123.bin\endcode

Do the same as in the first example, but track precisely what is going on:

\code{.sh}$ arcstk-parse --vvv dBAR-123.bin\endcode

Do the same as in the first example, but write to myfile.txt instead of stdout:

\code{.sh}$ arcstk-parse -o myfile.txt dBAR-123.bin\endcode


\section parse_bugs BUGS

\snippet{doc} include/text_bugs.dox    TEXT_BUGS


\section parse_copy COPYRIGHT

\snippet{doc} include/text_license.dox TEXT_LICENSE


\section parse_see SEE ALSO

@TOOL_NAME_ID@(1), @TOOL_NAME_CALC@(1), @TOOL_NAME_VERIFY@(1)

*/
